SOURCE corpus/SOURCES.md sha256=9715f44dca8dfc2beac94b17e19f0f0206b1efa4d973eb1183650a0f9179794f
# SOURCES — where tameshi learns

Where the lane's external reading lives: what each place teaches, how far to
trust it for which scope, and when to look again. Contract: `SOURCES-CONTRACT-v1.md`
(kaika, 2026-10-19). Admission of claims stays in `QUALITY.md`; this file holds
rows only, and a row is a claim opened in the round that writes it.

## Registry

| id | source | kind | tier | scope | anchor | teaches | status | opened | recheck | used-by |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| S001 | Mutant states and metrics (Stryker Mutator docs) — https://stryker-mutator.io/docs/mutation-testing-elements/mutant-states-and-metrics/ | docs | A | Stryker Mutator's own mutant-state and metric definitions | §Mutant states and §Metrics @ docs page fetched 2026-10-19 | eight mutant states; score = detected / valid x 100 with detected = killed + timeout; compile and runtime errors excluded; a separate score on covered code; test states killing, covering, not covering | mined | 2026-10-19 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/mutation-score-semantics.md, corpus/knowledge/mutation-case-kumitate-sources-check.md |
| S002 | mutation-testing-report-schema.json (stryker-mutator/mutation-testing-elements) — https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stryker-mutator/mutation-testing-elements/master/packages/report-schema/src/mutation-testing-report-schema.json | spec | A | cross-tool mutation report JSON schema | mutation-testing-report-schema.json:64-98 @ master, fetched 2026-10-19 | JSON Schema for cross-tool mutation reports: a status enum of 8 values, killedBy, coveredBy, statusReason and testsCompleted — a ready export shape for a kill-rate ledger | mined | 2026-10-19 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/mutation-score-semantics.md |
| S003 | Incremental (StrykerJS docs) — https://stryker-mutator.io/docs/stryker-js/incremental/ | docs | A | StrykerJS incremental verdict reuse | §Incremental mode and §Limitations @ docs page fetched 2026-10-19 | when a prior verdict may be reused, and the declared blind spots: env vars, dependencies and .snap files are not detected; the dry run stays required | mined | 2026-10-19 | 180d | corpus/knowledge/incremental-pin-disposition.md |
| S004 | cargo-mutants book: Using the results (also in-diff.html and iterate.html) — https://mutants.rs/using-results.html | docs | A | cargo-mutants outcome semantics and run-scoping options | §Tests fail in an clean tree? and §Mutant outcomes @ mutants.rs, fetched 2026-10-19 | outcomes caught, missed, unviable, timeout, with unviable called inconclusive; tests must first pass reliably in a copied tree; --in-diff and --iterate carry explicit cautions | mined | 2026-10-19 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/mutation-score-semantics.md, corpus/knowledge/repeated-control-precondition.md |
| S005 | mutmut changelog HISTORY.rst (boxed/mutmut) — https://raw.githubusercontent.com/boxed/mutmut/main/HISTORY.rst | code | A | mutmut's own recorded harness fixes | HISTORY.rst:13-46 (§3.8.0, §3.7.0) @ main, fetched 2026-10-19 | harness bugs the maintainers recorded, read as method lessons: CPU-time-limited mutants misreported as killed (fixed 3.8.0); env-clearing tests produced false survivors (fixed 3.8.0); per-function hash invalidation (3.7.0) | mined | 2026-10-19 | on-release | corpus/knowledge/mutation-score-semantics.md |
| S006 | shmutant README (BWBama85/shmutant) — https://github.com/BWBama85/shmutant | code | A | shmutant's own bash mutation verdict semantics | README §The three verdicts and §How a row is run @ page currentOid 7eefc73010ad6342b80e3ed43915503e02c90618, fetched 2026-10-19 | a row is old literal, replacement, witness; verdicts killed vs accidental, unapplied, baseline; a non-unique literal is refused; authoritative only for its own semantics (0 stars, 239 commits at open) | mined | 2026-10-19 | 90d | corpus/knowledge/witness-scoped-kill-verdict.md, corpus/knowledge/mutation-score-semantics.md, corpus/lessons/round-12.md |
